Proof-program takeaway:
  Automatic languages are good LRC packet filters only before scalarization.
  In this finite scout, the first 13 fibbinary and Moser-de Bruijn rows
  are not boundary threats: they have positive open safe mass at 1/14.
  AP and GW stay as zero-open denominator-14 boundary atoms.  The useful
  next theorem target is a DFA-labelled packet field for HYP-2963: automaton
  state, residue mod14, exact-period label, gap-block label, and first
  safe-component certificate or named F7/THM-572 residual.
